Cider: macdrv_set_window_mask() passed a Windows-coordinate rect to -[WineWindow setMask:],
which works in Mac coordinates. With Retina mode or a render scale the full-screen black bars then
covered most of the window. Convert it with cgrect_mac_from_win().

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -3379,7 +3379,9 @@
 @autoreleasepool
 {
     OnMainThread(^{
-        [window setMask:rect];
+        /* Cider: rect comes in Windows coordinates; convert it like every other rect
+           (only matters when Windows and Mac coordinates differ, i.e. Retina/render scale). */
+        [window setMask:cgrect_mac_from_win(rect)];
     });
 }
 }
